#X text 625 3119 Pitch Control;
#X text 669 3151 pitch_mode <0|1|2|3|4> - Off/Semitones/Range/Scale/MIDI;
#X text 669 3184 pitch_semitones <-24 to 24> - Fixed transposition;
#X text 669 3216 pitch_range <min> <max> - Semitone range;
#X text 669 3248 pitch_rand_type <type> - Random generator for pitch;
#X text 103 3534 pitch_rand_type <type> - Generator for pitch (rand_1-4 \, perlin_1d_1-4 \, etc.);
#X text 64 3630 Mode 0: OFF (default) \;;
#X text 103 3662 - Speed inlet/message controls speed directly \; - speed_range is active (if enabled \, speed value is replaced by random range) \; - Formula: speed = sample_param_range(speed_range \, speed_inlet) \; - Traditional granular playback with optional speed randomization \;;
#X text 64 3764 Mode 1: SEMITONES \;;
#X text 103 3809 - Speed inlet/message becomes the base pitch \; - speed_range is bypassed \; - Fixed semitone shift applied multiplicatively \; - Formula: final_speed = speed_inlet * 2^(semitones/12) \; - Messages: pitch_semitones <value> \; - Fixed pitch transposition (e.g. \, +7 semitones = perfect fifth up) \;;
#X text 64 3925 Mode 2: RANGE \;;
#X text 103 3969 - Speed inlet/message becomes the base pitch \; - speed_range is bypassed \; - Random semitone shift sampled from semitone_range \; - Formula: final_speed = speed_inlet * 2^(random_semitones/12) \; - Messages: pitch_range <min> <max> \, pitch_rand_type <rand_1|perlin_1d_1|lorenz_1|etc> \; - Random pitch variation within a semitone range \;;
#X text 64 4099 Mode 3: SCALE \;;
#X text 103 4130 - Speed inlet/message becomes the base pitch \; - speed_range is bypassed \; - Randomly picks a note from a predefined scale (list of semitone values) \; - Formula: final_speed = speed_inlet * 2^(scale_note/12) \; - Messages: pitch_scale <note1> <note2> ... <noteN> (up to 128 notes) \; - Quantized pitch selection (e.g. \, major scale: 0 2 4 5 7 9 11) \;;
#X text 68 4441 In modes 1-4 \, the speed parameter acts as a base reference pitch \, not a playback rate. The speed_range system is completely disabled in these modes. \;;
#X text 64 4275 Mode 4: MIDI \;;
#X text 103 4316 - Speed inlet/message becomes the base pitch (assumed to be middle C = 60) \; - speed_range is bypassed \; - MIDI note input (via signal inlet) transposes from base pitch \; - Formula: final_speed = speed_inlet * 2^((midi_note - 60)/12) \; - MIDI keyboard control \, assumes sample at base speed is tuned to C4 \;;
